\subsection{Horizontal wave output on paired underway replays}
\label{sec:wave-readout-replay}
We compared Eq.~\eqref{eq:horizontal-wave-readout} with the recursive
position and velocity on identical wave and sensor histories. Eight
records in each sea direction span JONSWAP and PM--Stokes seas at
$H_s=0.27$, $1.5$, $4$, and $8.5$ m. Each displacement RMS uses all
180,000 samples from 300 to 1,200 s. We pooled records with equal weight
by taking the square root of the mean squared record RMS.

On the standard sensor draw, across both gyro sampling profiles, pooled
3-D displacement RMS fell from 0.434 to 0.349 m. North and east RMS fell
from 0.299 to 0.228 m and from 0.249 to 0.184 m, respectively. With the
default gyro profile, 3-D velocity RMS fell from 0.0782 to 0.0661 m/s.
The paired heave, attitude and bias scores were identical on the two
profiles. At 40--60 s the displacement outputs also agreed. This
timing locates the displacement gain after the bias-learning gate opens.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
