On the two reserved draws, pooled 3-D displacement RMS fell from
0.433 to 0.349 m (19.39\%, Fig.~\ref{fig:ou3-wave-readout-pairs}).
Eight rough-sea replays with simulated engine vibration gave 0.879 and
0.711 m. In the low--high--low transition, following-sea RMS fell from
0.407 to 0.350 m and head-sea RMS from 0.333 to 0.265 m.
The wave records are shared across sensor draws. The numerical comparison
and its reproduction settings are available with the
\href{https://github.com/bareboat-necessities/ocean-imu/tree/fee96e2b3be2d3d9d67b654f76ebea92b291df57/reports/results/startup_learning/ou3_wave_motion}{paired replay data}.

% BEGIN paired production wave phase study
\paragraph{Independent phase and sensor draws}
Each sea direction has ten draws on four JONSWAP records, four PM--Stokes records
and one changing-sea record. We compared the estimator on \texttt{main} at
\texttt{cee633f} with the production filter using byte-identical generated inputs.
Table~\ref{tab:ou3-production-phase} pools the per-record 3-D displacement RMS
over equal $300$--$1200$ s windows. The last column counts draws with lower 3-D RMS.
